# <type>(<scope>): <subject>            <-- 50 chars max, imperative, no full stop
#
# <body>                                <-- wrap at 72; explain WHY, not what
#
# <footer>                              <-- Refs #123 / Closes #123 / BREAKING CHANGE:
#
# ── type ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat      a new capability visible to a user or admin
#   fix       a bug fix
#   perf      a performance improvement
#   refactor  code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   style     formatting only (Pint) — no logic change
#   test      adding or correcting tests
#   docs      documentation only
#   build     dependencies, Vite, Composer, npm
#   ci        GitHub Actions, deployment pipeline
#   chore     housekeeping that fits nothing above
#   revert    reverts a previous commit
#
# ── scope (optional but encouraged) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#   donations shop cms admin auth theme seo payments sms email deploy infra
#
# ── examples ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat(donations): add cover-the-transaction-fee toggle
#   fix(payments): verify webhook against raw body, not parsed input
#   ci(deploy): pin known_hosts on port 2222
#
# ── rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   * Never commit secrets. .env is ignored; .env.example documents every key.
#   * Anything touching money, auth or webhooks ships with Pest tests.
#   * BREAKING CHANGE: in the footer for anything requiring a manual server step.
